Every substance-use-disorder-treatment-specialist is an opioid-use-disorder-care-provider.
Every SAMHSA-certified-opioid-treatment-program is an opioid-use-disorder-care-provider.
Every office-based-buprenorphine-treatment-provider is a substance-use-disorder-treatment-specialist.
Every office-based-naltrexone-treatment-provider is a substance-use-disorder-treatment-specialist.
Every SAMHSA-certified-opioid-treatment-program may provide a methadone-treatment.
Every SAMHSA-certified-opioid-treatment-program may provide a buprenorphine-treatment.
If a patient has an opioid-use-disorder and a clinician cannot provide an opioid-use-disorder-treatment for the patient then the clinician should arrange an opioid-use-disorder-care for the patient from an opioid-use-disorder-care-provider.
If a patient has an opioid-use-disorder and a clinician cannot provide an opioid-use-disorder-treatment for the patient then the clinician may arrange an opioid-use-disorder-care for the patient from a substance-use-disorder-treatment-specialist.
If a patient has an opioid-use-disorder and a clinician cannot provide an opioid-use-disorder-treatment for the patient then the clinician may arrange an opioid-use-disorder-care for the patient from a SAMHSA-certified-opioid-treatment-program.
